# Time Complexity
### Counting Ones
```
O(n)
```
### Building Blocks
```
O(n)
```
### Traversing Blocks
```
O(n)
```
Overall
```
O(n)
```
---
# Space Complexity
The lists storing the blocks can contain at most `n` groups.
```
O(n)
```
---
# Key Observation (Most Important)
When we remove
```
00011100
```
it becomes
```
00000000
```
The left and right zero blocks merge with the removed one block.
Therefore,
```
Merged Zero Length
= Left Zero + One Block + Right Zero
```
After flipping,
```
Gain
= (Left + One + Right) - One
= Left + Right
```
So the **net increase** depends **only** on the neighboring zero blocks.
> **Final Formula**
```
Answer = Original Ones + Maximum(Left Zero Length + Right Zero Length)
```
This observation allows us to solve the problem in **O(n)** time without actually modifying the string.
